{
  "feature": "About visual PR 3 to PR 6a: /about/[area], the strip, On this page, the labelled screen, Good to know, Try it, the ways in (the index and the ?), and the launches on Home's banner (PR 6b)",
  "note": "PR 3 to PR 5 rows are gotos; PR 6a's rows open the index and press the ? from one screen per area (`openHelp`), each landing under its back bar. Reads only; no clearAbout (the database is read-only for this walk). The decks rows press the Lock cards label (needs NEVER_CUT_ENABLED on for the account) and photograph its lit region, pin and line. PR 4 rows scroll each section that carries rules to its Good to know block ([data-good-to-know=<section id>]): phone draws a swipe row (dots only with two or more cards), desktop a grid of three. The friends row scrolls to the bottom: every Friends rule follows a Friends switch that is off for the reader, so no Good to know heading should be drawn there. PR 5 rows: Try it under the Analysis section (phone draws one card and N more below, which the second row presses; desktop a row of three), and a Show me landing on Proposed cuts (lit label; New tag and card only when the audit account has not been told about it, so either state is a pass if it matches the seen state). PR 6b rows photograph Home's banner as the account's About row stands, so each needs its own state and the run that photographs one leaves the other red: set the row to `pnpm probe:about-banner`'s ONE state (the floor, every catalog id and unit key, less `decks/your-deck/lock` and `locked-cards`) for about-banner-one, and its TWO state (less `rule/lock` too) for about-banner-two, with NEVER_CUT_ENABLED on; the probe itself presses both, and ✕ and Show me.",
